+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,20 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "./src/index.js";
+
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": 1 }, "/a~1b"); // 1 (`~1` is "/", `~0` is "~")
+resolvePointer(doc, ""); // the whole document
+```
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the referenced value (not a copy; the document is never
+mutated). It throws an `Error` when the pointer is not valid (non-empty without a leading `/`, or a bad
+`~` escape), or when it does not resolve: missing member, out-of-range or malformed array index (leading
+zeros, signs), the `-` index, or descending into a scalar. Only own members are resolved, so
+`__proto__`, `constructor` and the like cannot reach the prototype chain. The URI fragment form
+(`#/foo`) of RFC 6901 section 6 is not supported.
